    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498328/degree-works-specialist": {
      "title": "Degree Works Specialist",
      "description": "Degree Works Specialist Apply now Job no: 498328 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Administrative, Staff Position Title: Degree Works Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 61200 - Registrar Advertised Salary: $54.194. See Job Summary for details on salary placement. Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Admin / Admin Temp Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Primary responsibilities include programming for Ferris' degree audit platform, MyDegree (Degree Works by Ellucian). This position documents curricular changes, generates reports, reviews curriculum proposals, and provides customer service for MyDegree. This is a full-time, continuing position. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H-1 B, etc. experience, and internal pay equity considerations. The salary grade for this position is 9 Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors: Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position. Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role. Upper Range: Candidates with seven or more years of directly related experience, advanced knowledge, specialized skills, certifications, or expertise that provide significant value to the position. Final compensation will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelor’s degree. Required Work Experience: Two years of professional office experience. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Demonstrated work experience in higher education using an enterprise software program. Familiarity with academic advising and student records. Exposure to post-secondary curriculum processes and procedures. Experience with Degree Works or other degree audit platforms in the test environment. Knowledge of Ferris general education requirements. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Work collaboratively across the institution to program Degree Works using the Ellucian scribing language to scribe academic program and technical requirements. • Analyze and troubleshoot system problems concerning degree audits. • Review current processes, evaluate, and implement changes for improvement. • Provide assistance to faculty, staff, and students, and serve as a liaison to other key departments for degree audit evaluations for all degree programs. • Maintain records (e.g., logs, notes, correspondence, memoranda, and reports) to ensure accurate, efficient, and effective operation of the automated degree audit system. • Assist in creating documentation and training materials to assist faculty & staff with Degree Works-specific duties. • Serve as the Scribe for all academic programs and curricular changes in collaboration with the RAM team (Registrar's Office, Academic Affairs, & MyDegree). • Interact with Academic Affairs, the University Curriculum Committee, IT personnel, and degree program representatives to create accurate degree audits for all Ferris State University degree programs, minors, and certificates. • Participate in the work of the MyDegree Advisory Board, especially the testing procedures. • Maintain functional knowledge of Ferris curriculum/graduation requirements, including general education requirements. • Follow all procedures as outlined in the DegreeWorks Configuration & Release documentation manuals. • Maintain confidentiality of student records in compliance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA). • Stay current with new releases of MyDegree by researching scribe techniques, participating in the Ellucian E-Commons, and other activities that keep Ferris' scribing current. • Generate Transit reports to identify which academic programs use courses affected by curriculum proposals. • Update and maintain the MyDegree departmental website. • Assist in the monitoring of the MyDegree departmental e-mail and respond to questions as needed. • Assist in answering the MyDegree support line and assist users as needed. • Maintain the Academic Affairs Checksheet Repository by creating and uploading the correct and current checksheets for each program and adding new programs when approved through the curriculum process. • Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. • Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. • Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. • Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. • Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: • Write basic computer code. • Competent in Excel, Word, and databases, preferably SQL. • Learn new software related to higher education and retention. • Communicate effectively in written and oral forms to multiple audiences. • Organize work to accomplish tasks by the deadline. • Work independently. • Explore progressive uses of systems related to degree auditing. • Think critically in a team environment. • Focus on solving complex problems with attention to detail. • Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of the unofficial transcript of their Bachelor’s degree. The transcript must include the institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, and degree awarded. Finalists must submit an official transcript. Initial Application Review Date: October 26, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498329/plumbing-boiler-plant-supervisor": {
      "title": "Plumbing & Boiler Plant Supervisor",
      "description": "Plumbing & Boiler Plant Supervisor Apply now Job no: 498329 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Administrative, Staff Position Title: Plumbing & Boiler Plant Supervisor Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55503 - Plumbing Advertised Salary: $76,707. See Job Summary for details on salary placement. Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Admin / Admin Temp Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Provide leadership, oversight, training, performance management, and professional development for the Plumbing and Boiler Plant shops. Supervise and coordinate the work activities of the plumbers and boiler operators engaged in the operations and maintenance of plumbing systems and the Boiler Plant, including steam distribution systems. Operations of the Plant include operating, monitoring, and maintaining plant equipment and plumbing systems to ensure reliable, safe, and efficient operations of the Boiler Plant and campus Plumbing systems. This includes high-pressure boilers and auxiliary equipment that use natural gas as the primary fuel source to ensure continuous, reliable, and critical steam service to facilities located on the University’s campus. Operations and maintenance of the steam distribution and domestic hot water systems, including operating, monitoring, and maintaining distribution systems. Serve as project manager for contracted and in-house maintenance, construction, and renovation projects related to the Plumbing and Boiler Plant departments. Coordinate with contracted partners and University staff to maintain required regulatory information, coordinate required inspections, and coordinate vendor support. This position is located in Big Rapids, Michigan, and the anticipated shift will be M-F, 8:00 am – 4:30 pm. Assignment requires availability to work weekend and evening shifts as needed and to respond to emergency calls. Offers are determined based on a review of the candidate's qualifications, including education, training, experience, and internal pay equity considerations. Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors: Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position. Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role. Upper Range: Candidates with seven or more years of directly related experience, advanced knowledge, specialized skills, certifications, or expertise that provide significant value to the position. Final compensation will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H-1 B, etc. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: Minimum three years of supervisory experience related to plumbing operations or boiler plant operations. Required Licenses and Certifications: State of Michigan Master Plumber license. Valid driver’s license. Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Carrying Electrical Hazards Inclement Weather Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Climbing Driving Heights Lifting Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Associate's degree or higher from an accredited institution. Supervisory experience within an educational institution, hospital, K-12 institution, or commercial accounts. OSHA Safety certification, APPA or other facilities management certification, and documented leadership development training. Operation of Boilers and associated systems. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Supervise, train, schedule, and approve vacation/sick/personal leave requests; evaluate and assign work to Plumbers, Boiler Plant operators, apprentice plumbers/boiler operators, and student workers to maintain an appropriate response level within the departments and meet campus needs. Oversee the field hours of our Plumber I and Plumber II plumbers. Ensure their work meets state regulatory standards, track their progress, and officially sign off on their logged man-hours so they can qualify for their Journeyman or Master Plumber licensing exams. Assign jobs, maintain quality control, monitor work progress, and ensure that safety procedures are followed. Maintain the overtime list, pager list, timecards, and labor distribution information as needed to ensure the IWMS work order system and time management system are accurate. Analyze jobs and work order requests to plan material, labor, and time requirements, and provide cost estimates as needed. Coordinate with other department supervisors to expedite work completion. Coordinate and manage planned and unplanned outages for boilers, steam distribution, hot-water distribution, and plumbing systems. Respond to emergencies and direct workforce activities at all times (may include being available to respond 365 days a year, 24 hours a day, if necessary). Instruct employees in the use of new products and equipment. Perform facility audits to determine current and future deferred maintenance and minor capital improvement requirements. Make rounds of buildings to inspect work and correct problems. Provide engineering and design support for maintenance and construction projects related to the Boiler Plant, steam distribution, domestic hot water distribution systems, other water distribution systems, and plumbing systems. Work with the City of Big Rapids as required. Review work orders and project requests for labor and material needs, and provide cost estimates as needed. Coordinate with Stores to arrange for the order and delivery of materials as required. Evaluate and ensure conformance with all applicable plumbing/mechanical/boiler/building codes. Interact with salespeople and vendors as needed to stay abreast of new products and contractor performance. Update and maintain University standards related to the Boiler Plant, steam distribution systems, domestic hot water distribution systems, and Plumbing systems. Maintain all CSD-1 testing/inspections for all boilers and work with the State of Michigan as required. Maintain backflow testing and documentation, including coordination with a 3rd-party entity and the City of Big Rapids as required. Maintain records and prepare various reports as required. Maintain the safety and security of the boiler plant, plumbing storage areas, and equipment. Attend meetings, write memos and letters as required. Attend seminars and conferences to stay current with industry trends and technology, and participate in technical training to enhance knowledge and skills. Administer and ensure compliance with work rules and the Union contract. Evaluate department staff performance and assess employees' skill levels to meet the department's goals, operations, and maintenance objectives. Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Reports directly to the Director of Operations. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Must be able to lead, coordinate, and create a positive work environment for all assigned employees. Read and interpret construction drawing/prints, charts, and job specifications. Skills and Abilities: Must have basic computer skills needed to perform tasks in the time management system, the IWMS, and other University systems. Must have working knowledge of Boiler, Mechanical, plumbing, and other related building codes. Must be able to motivate, organize, schedule, and supervise employees. Must be able to establish and maintain effective interpersonal relationships; communicate effectively (both orally and in writing); perform basic mathematical functions accurately; evaluate the performance, personality, adaptability, and skill levels of job applicants and employees; and understand and administer union contracts and labor relations. Must possess a positive attitude, be adaptable to changing priorities and technological changes within the industry, and be able to lead and provide guidance to department employees. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Certification/License Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 26, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498330/public-safety-dispatcher": {
      "title": "Public Safety Dispatcher",
      "description": "Public Safety Dispatcher Apply now Job no: 498330 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Clerical Position Title: Public Safety Dispatcher Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 57000 - Public Safety Advertised Salary: $19.66 Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and CTA/MEA-NEA Agreement Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Clerical Tech Association (CTA) FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Clerical-Technical Association (MEA-NEA) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Under the direction of the Director of Public Safety, this position manages the Public Safety communication system, monitors campus-wide security cameras, maintains after-hours access control, and performs various police records support functions, some of which require special certification. These positions will have a 4-day work week and a 10-hour workday, with a shift differential of $.30 per hour, as defined in the CTA/MEA contract. Work hours for these positions are 3:00 pm – 2:00 am, with a one-hour unpaid lunch period. The work schedules for these positions are as follows: Dispatcher 1/Week 1 – Sunday, Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday. Week 2 – Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, and Saturday. Dispatcher 2/Week 1 – Monday, Tuesday, Friday, and Saturday. Week 2 – Sunday, Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Required Work Experience: Office experience. Required Licenses and Certifications: LEIN certified or achieve such certification within 60 days of hire. Physical Demands: Office Environment Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Repetitive movement Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Associate’s degree One year of police dispatcher experience. Formal training in law enforcement and/or dispatching related discipline. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Answer incoming calls and direct communications to the proper destination and/or assign the appropriate response service, such as dispatching police officers to non-emergency complaints and referring emergency police, fire, and EMS requests to Central Dispatch. • Coordinate police response and services to University students, faculty, and staff as needed. • Monitor and coordinate response to intrusion, hold-up, and fire alarm systems. • Type, keyboard, input, record, and file records according to established procedures. • Responsible for monitoring the campus-wide security camera system. • Maintain after-hours access control for University buildings. • Upon authorization to do so, will initiate and notify constituents via the emergency mass communication system in various emergencies. • Review forms and other documents to ensure proper completion. • Retrieve and input data utilizing a computer and printer. • Certified LEIN operator. • Process abandoned vehicle reports. • Process traffic citations. • Assist General Counsel with FOIA requests. • Conduct background checks for other agencies. • Process requests for police reports. • Maintain confidentiality as required by law and department procedures. • Prepare/coordinate department/University mail/document deliveries. • Responsible for tracking and appropriately dispatching the Public Safety Officers. • Response/coordination of DPS communication in emergencies/mass casualties/disasters. • Maintains the department’s records system, as directed. • Report directly to the Director of Public Safety. • Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. • Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. • Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. • Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. • Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Register hunting firearms. Skills and Abilities: • Maintain composure in crisis situations and be able to work under the pressure of an emergency. • Communicate effectively and be able to successfully interact in unusual situations and with difficult customers. • Use computer software such as word-processing, spreadsheets, databases, and other management software. • Successfully interact with visitors, staff, faculty, and students. • Able to share sensitive information on a need-to-know basis only. • Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Transcripts Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 23, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498331/lead-print-specialist": {
      "title": "Lead Print Specialist",
      "description": "Lead Print Specialist Apply now Job no: 498331 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Clerical Position Title: Lead Print Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 51100 - Printing Services Advertised Salary: $23.43 Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and CTA/MEA-NEA Agreement. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Clerical Tech Association (CTA) FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Clerical-Technical Association (MEA-NEA) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: The position involves operating digital and large format printing equipment and all associate activities, taking part in management of campus copier fleet and covering for manager when that person is out of the office Position Type: Staff Required Education: Associate’s Degree in Printing/Graphic Media or related field. Satisfactory completion of two years of college or equivalent. The listed requirements represent the knowledge, skills, and/or abilities required. Any equivalent combination of education, training, and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities may be considered. Equivalency for education: Two years of full-time, related work experience equals one year of education. Required Work Experience: Two years of part-time work are equivalent to one year of full-time work. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Carrying Reaching Sitting Twisting Climbing Driving Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Full-time experience with traditional print equipment, digital print and large-format equipment, and all associated support systems, including installation of large-format signage Graphic Design Experience Demonstrated experience with university systems such as Banner, Concur, etc. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: - Operates digital printing equipment and associated bindery equipment. - Operates large-format printing equipment and associated finishing equipment. - Performs installation of large-format projects as necessary. - Schedules and prepares projects for printing and production using associated prepress and design programs such as Adobe products, Canva, Microsoft products, etc. - Use MIS printing programs such as PrintSmith and Fiery. - Organize workload to efficiently meet promised delivery dates. - Recognize, analyze, troubleshoot, and make minor repairs to equipment. Contact service personnel, explain the problem in detail, and arrange repairs. - Maintain adequate supply of paper and supplies, order if necessary, and ensure accuracy of materials inventory in the MIS system. - Ensure the security of tests and confidential materials. - Ensure the high quality of completed products. - Provide lead support for the copier fleet and student printing programs on campus, working with others to provide services needed and with other departments to assist with support, installation, and maintenance of the copier fleet. - Process reports for monthly chargebacks and upload to accounting. - Monitor equipment and place calls for maintenance or service as required. - Train and direct the work of student employees and part-time employees. - Coordinate work assignments for full-time staff when needed. - Maintain Concur and Banner records and prepare monthly balancing reports. - Open and close the facility. - Operate a cash register; balance daily receipts with cash sheets; prepare bank deposits. - Report directly to the Print Services Manager. - Perform certain duties to back up the Print Services Manager in the case of the manager's absence. - Promote customer awareness of the variety of services provided - Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. - Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. - Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. - Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. - Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. - Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: Communicate effectively. Demonstrated logical and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated knowledge of a printing operation and equipment. Plan and utilize materials and supplies economically. Supervise student employees. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of their degree, if applicable. If you do not have a transcript, please write a justification explaining how your work experience is equivalent to the required education, and attach it instead of the transcript. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. The individual hired will be required to submit an official transcript (if applicable). Initial Application Review Date: October 26, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498333/temporary-auto-mechanic": {
      "title": "Temporary Auto Mechanic",
      "description": "Temporary Auto Mechanic Apply now Job no: 498333 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Temporary Auto Mechanic Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55301 - Transportation Services Advertised Salary: $24.35-hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement Benefits: Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Temporary Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Perform skilled trades work in repairing and maintaining University owned and leased vehicles, heavy equipment and small engines. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: Three years full-time equivalent automotive mechanic experience in licensed recognized automotive repair facility. Required Licenses and Certifications: Valid driver’s license. Michigan certification or ASE equivalent in at least four categories of the first eight categories in automotive and light truck repair. Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Twisting Balancing Driving Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Michigan certification or ASE equivalent in one or more of the first six categories in heavy duty truck repair. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Diagnose and analyze problems utilizing automotive computerized electrical diagnostic systems. Fabricate and repair using welding equipment. Keep accurate records and procure related parts. Maintain assigned tools, equipment, and work area in a neat, organized, and clean, non-hazardous environment. Perform minor body repairs. Rebuild transmissions and repair and/or replace hydraulic transmission systems. Repair automotive electrical and hydraulic systems. Repair, mount, and balance tires; work on related areas of the vehicle's suspension system. Tune up and overhaul all types of engines, including the use of required welding equipment. Maintain the safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories. Maintain safety, health, and quality standards and comply with various regulations in all duties and responsibilities. Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Assist other service workers as needed. Train and work with others in the performance of the characteristic duties. Skills and Abilities: Diagnose and analyze using automotive computerized electrical equipment. Direct, train, and work with mechanic intern students, automotive apprentices, and others in performing the characteristic duties. Keep and maintain accurate records. Maintain University standards of good workmanship in both quality and quantity. Perform skilled work in the repair and maintenance of vehicles, heavy equipment, commercial/industrial farm tractors, and small engines. Read, understand, and follow directions, safety labels, and equipment operation manuals. Understand and know the methods, materials, tools, equipment, occupational hazards, and safety precautions of the trade. Understand, use good judgment, and follow procedures established through safety training and the physical plant safety manual. Use welding equipment. Work harmoniously with others in situations involving variable temperatures, occasional noise, stressful workloads, and inclement weather. Work independently. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Certification/License Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 26, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498334/figure-model": {
      "title": "Figure Model",
      "description": "Figure Model Apply now Job no: 498334 Work type: Staff Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Staff, Part-Time Position Title: Figure Model Location: Grand Rapids (Kendall) Department: 45000 - KCAD Dean's Office Advertised Salary: $22 per hour Benefits: Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Part Time Support FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Temporary Part-Time/Full-Time: Part-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 9 Month (non-faculty) At Will/Just Cause: At Will Summary of Position: Provide in classroom figure modeling services for classes at Ferris State University’s Kendall College of Art and Design’s campus in Grand Rapids, Michigan. The figure model will pose in a studio setting for educational purposes. Poses may be unclothed or clothed, allowing students to study the human form from observation. Please note, most class requirements will require unclothed posing. This position requires the ability to hold poses for extended periods and remain focused and engaged during the session. This is a part-time, on-call position not to exceed 28 hours per week. Students currently enrolled in any program at Ferris State University will not be considered for this position. The anticipated start date of this position is late November 2026. However, this is an estimated date and can be revised if needed. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High School diploma or equivalent Required Work Experience: Previous modeling experience/knowledge of figure modeling techniques preferred but not required. Must be 18 years of age. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Bending Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Experience creating sequential or consecutive poses. Familiarity with the visual arts. Experience in sports, dance, theater, or other forms of stylized movement. Experience working in a professional academic setting. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Following direction from the instructor, provide a range of poses, from gestures to sustained poses, that may include static and dynamic positions for extended periods of time. Maintain a respectful distance from students and student work. Clearly understand the role and that there are to be no relationships with students. Demonstrate a range of body movements and positions within physical comfort and ability, allowing artists to study different angles and muscle groups. Maintain a focused and composed demeanor while posing, respecting the creative process and the privacy of the studio environment. Communicate with the instructor to clarify pose requests or address any concerns. Dress appropriately for the instructor and the class assignment. Arrive on time for scheduled sessions. Models are expected to arrive 10-15 minutes before their scheduled session to prepare and be ready to pose at the start of class. This position requires someone with a very flexible schedule, as hours vary daily based on specific classroom needs. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Basic knowledge of human anatomy and the ability to control body positioning. Comfort with posing in front of others, including being nude or in a partially nude state. Demonstrated commitment, experience, and understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion. Willingness to receive and implement feedback from instructors in a collaborative environment and adapt to different pose requests. Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 26, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU. Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498324/tour-guide-student-position": {
      "title": "Tour Guide (Student Position)",
      "description": "Tour Guide (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498324 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Tour Guide (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Department: Enrollment Services Advertised Salary: $13.73 Summary of Position: Do you enjoy public speaking and answering questions? If so, becoming a tour guide allows you to do just that, with a flexible schedule. Tour Guides will give walking tours of campus, escort groups to and from various campus locations, and share their love of Ferris to prospective students that are coming to visit in a large group from schools or organizations. Based on semester, Tour Guides will also have a role with the Crimson and Gold program and Orientation. Position Requirements: *Possess good public speaking skills *Have strong knowledge of the University and be able to answer a variety of questions *Must be comfortable with working outdoors *Need at least 2 semesters of education at Ferris Essential Duties/Responsibilities: *Offer presentations or campus tours *Escort students and chaperones to various locations across campus *Work campus events and Orientation programming *Be able to walk a mile while talking Additional Physical Requirements: Being able to walk at least a mile while talking. Number of Positions Available: 30 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Class Schedule Job Close Date: February 13, 2027 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 13 Feb 2027 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498321/makerspace-helper-student-position": {
      "title": "Makerspace Helper (Student Position)",
      "description": "Makerspace Helper (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498321 Work type: Student Employment - Work Study Only Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - Work Study Only Position Title: Makerspace Helper (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Department: College of Engineering Technology Advertised Salary: $14.00 Summary of Position: Assist students and faculty with design and fabrication projects, train users on 3D printers and laser equipment, and maintain makerspace tools and supplies to support hands-on learning. Position Type: Student Employment - Work Study Only Position Requirements: Ability to: Operate and maintain 3D printers, laser cutters, and related equipment. Follow and promote safety procedures while keeping machines in good working order. Train and assist students and faculty in using makerspace tools. Troubleshoot issues with equipment and projects as needed. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Keep the makerspace running day to day and make sure equipment is ready to use. Run and maintain 3D printers, laser cutters, and other tools. Help students and faculty with their projects, from setup to troubleshooting. Show people how to use the machines safely and correctly. Keep track of supplies and let supervisors know when things are running low. Make sure the space stays safe, clean, and organized. Work with people from different programs and support a variety of projects. Number of Positions Available: 2 Documents Needed to Apply: Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 16, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 07 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498319/payroll-office-assistant-student-position": {
      "title": "Payroll Office Assistant (Student Position)",
      "description": "Payroll Office Assistant (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498319 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Payroll Office Assistant (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: Payroll Advertised Salary: $13.73- $13.99 Summary of Position: Processing payroll information, working with payroll staff. Position Requirements: Required skills include keying accuracy, basic math, Excel, organization and people skills. Professionalism, discretion, and confidentiality are expected. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Duties include filing, typing, greeting employees at front desk, answering phones, passing out and assisting employees with Payroll forms, assisting with Pick Ups, editing, checking computer entries, scanning and assisting other departments as well as other duties as assigned. Number of Positions Available: 1 Documents Needed to Apply: Cover Letter/Resume/Class Schedule Job Close Date: October 30, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
