    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498286/pharmacy-research-internasst-student-position": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Research Intern/Asst (Student Position)",
      "description": "Pharmacy Research Intern/Asst (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498286 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Pharmacy Research Intern/Asst (Student Position) Location: Grand Rapids, MI Department: College of Pharmacy Advertised Salary: $14.49 Summary of Position: Support clinical research activities across all phases of study development and execution. Responsibilities include completion of required research compliance and training; assisting with institutional review board (IRB) submissions and documentation; identifying and screening eligible study cases; conducting electronic medical record chart reviews to extract and enter study variables into data management software; performing basic statistical analyses; and contributing to dissemination of findings through abstract and manuscript development for presentation and publication. Position Requirements: Enrolled in the PharmD program Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Complete all required research and regulatory training to support study conduct and compliance. Assist with preparation and submission of Institutional Review Board (IRB) applications and related study documentation. Identify and screen eligible study participants/cases according to established inclusion and exclusion criteria. Perform electronic health record (EHR) chart review to collect, abstract, and accurately enter study variables into designated data management platforms. Conduct basic statistical analyses and assist with interpretation of study findings. Contribute to dissemination of research through preparation and development of abstracts, posters, presentations, and/or manuscripts for scholarly publication. Number of Positions Available: 3 Documents Needed to Apply: Job Close Date: October 8, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 05 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 17 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498312/fashion-studies-studio-lab-tech-student-position": {
      "title": "Fashion Studies Studio Lab Tech (Student Position)",
      "description": "Fashion Studies Studio Lab Tech (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498312 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Fashion Studies Studio Lab Tech (Student Position) Location: Grand Rapids, MI Department: Kendall College of Art and Design Advertised Salary: $13.73 Summary of Position: Lab tech for Fashion Studies open sewing lab Mondays and Wednesdays 6:00pm to 9:00pm. Possible Tuesday/Thursday hours. Position Requirements: Fashion Studies student Knows the sewing machines Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Keep the studios clean and organized during open lab hours Make sure sewing machines and surgers are running properly. If a machine is not running properly, let the instructor know Other help to students working in the lab Number of Positions Available: 2 Documents Needed to Apply: Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 30, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 05 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
