    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498315/admissionsorientation-team-lead-student-position": {
      "title": "Admissions/Orientation Team Lead (Student Position)",
      "description": "Admissions/Orientation Team Lead (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498315 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Admissions/Orientation Team Lead (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: Student Affairs: Enrollment Services Advertised Salary: $14.00-$14.49 Summary of Position: Do you have a strong interest in leadership, organization, and student success? Join the Admissions and Orientation Student Leadership Team and contribute to creating a positive and welcoming experience for prospective and incoming Ferris State University students. In this role, you will provide leadership and guidance to a team of student employees, supporting daily operations and serving as a point of contact within your designated functional area. This position includes cross-training in Tours, Communications, and Orientation, with a primary focus in one area. The role is designed to promote collaboration, inclusivity, and professional development while supporting the university’s enrollment and transition efforts. Position Type: Student Position Position Requirements: Current Ferris State University student in good academic standing Demonstrated leadership experience, including the ability to lead, train, or mentor peers Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple responsibilities Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team Commitment to providing a welcoming, inclusive, and student-centered experience Reliability, professionalism, and the ability to serve as a positive role model Availability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings, weekends, and summer employment as required by departmental needs Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Lead and mentor a team of student employees, fostering a professional, inclusive, and collaborative work environment Assist with onboarding, training, and ongoing development of student staff Create, manage, and adjust student employee schedules to ensure adequate coverage for daily operations and events Conduct regular audits and quality checks to ensure accuracy, compliance, and consistency with departmental standards Manage inventory, including tracking, organizing, and replenishing materials and supplies Serve as a primary point of communication between professional staff and student employees, relaying information clearly and effectively Lead and facilitate team meetings, trainings, and briefings to ensure alignment and preparedness Support the planning, coordination, and execution of admissions and orientation events, including summer and weekends as needed Oversee printing, processing, and distribution of materials related to admissions, tours, and orientation Assist with basic design and preparation of communications and materials in alignment with university branding standards Process forms, requests, and documentation accurately and in a timely manner Maintain professionalism and represent Ferris State University positively when interacting with prospective students, families, and campus partners Support cross-functional operations through collaboration with Tours, Communications, and Orientation teams Additional Physical Requirements Ability to walk extended distances (up to 1.5 miles) while speaking, providing information, and engaging with groups during campus tours and events. Number of Positions Available: 4 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 05 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
