    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498285/assistant-professor-sales-and-marketing-academic-year-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Sales and Marketing (Academic Year, Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Sales and Marketing (Academic Year, Tenure Track) Apply now Job no: 498285 Work type: Faculty - Temporary & Continuing Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Faculty Position Title: Assistant Professor - Sales and Marketing (Academic Year, Tenure Track) Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 34500 - Marketing Advertised Salary: $95,000 to $105,000; Salary commensurate with qualifications pursuant to the FFA Agreement. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Faculty Health Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Ferris Faculty Association (MEA-NEA) Term of Position: Academic Year At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: The College of Business at Ferris State University seeks a diverse group of outstanding applicants for a full-time, academic-year, tenure-track Assistant Professor - Sales and Marketing position. Teaching various undergraduate courses in sales-related courses (e.g., Professional Selling, Sales Management, and Advanced Selling). Teaching may include undergraduate and graduate courses. The candidate will help develop and improve curriculum and delivery, assess student learning, and contribute to service work, including student engagement activities and committees, and will engage in scholarly activities and professional development aligned with current and emerging programmatic needs. The candidate will help grow and expand the sales program. Faculty members have professional responsibilities, including advising students, serving on committees, maintaining regularly posted office hours, engaging in professional development, and participating in traditional functions of academic significance. Candidates are expected to foster a meaningful learning experience for our students; faculty are expected to be student-oriented, advise, and integrate current technology into the learning environment. Additionally, faculty will participate in collaborative efforts to advance curricular initiatives, assess student learning, and further develop programmatic enhancements. Specifically, we expect the candidate to be willing to engage students outside the classroom, support and expand our existing academic initiatives, and mentor students beyond a traditional academic advising role. In support of teaching, candidates will engage in scholarly/professional activities and participate in department, college, and university committees. Courses are to be taught in person on one of Ferris State University's Campuses or approved FSU sites. Faculty members may be required to teach off-campus and/or online. The candidate selected for the position must reside in Michigan after acceptance of employment and will perform duties at a Ferris site. The anticipated start date of this position is January 2027 at the earliest and August 2027 at the latest. The selected candidate must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Position Type: Faculty - Temporary & Continuing Required Education: A master’s degree in business with a marketing or sales concentration; OR A related master’s degree with 18 graduate credit hours in marketing or sales. Required Work Experience: Business-to-business sales experience is required. Candidates with experience teaching in a classroom setting and the ability to employ multiple teaching modalities, such as face-to-face, online, and blended strategies, to enhance student engagement and understanding are highly desirable. Candidates must be committed to continuous improvement in teaching and active participation in scholarly and professional development activities to adapt to changing industry needs. Candidates must demonstrate effective communication skills and personal initiative while working both independently and collaboratively. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Carrying Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: A PhD or DBA in Marketing, with an emphasis in sales or a similar field, is desirable but not required. If the doctorate is in a related area, 18 graduate hours in marketing are required. Alternate modality college-level teaching experience (e.g., hy-flex, online, mixed delivery). Industry experience in marketing or a closely related field. Practical industry experience in business-to-business sales is desirable. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Teach full-time during the academic year. Teach four courses per semester. Teach and coordinate elective courses in areas of expertise. Course topics will be assigned based on the credentials required to teach them. The courses the sales faculty member may be asked to teach may include, but are not limited to, Professional Selling, Sales Management, and Advanced Selling. Recruit students (including Dawg Days, Admitted Student Days, visits to high schools or career tech centers, and other University-outreach events) throughout the academic year, including some Saturdays. Serve on program committees and represent the program(s) on College and University committees. Collaborate with faculty on curriculum development, assessment, and quality assurance of assigned coursework. Maintain records and conduct assessments, advising, and all other administrative functions of the position in accordance with policies and procedures developed by the university, college, school, department, and/or program. Employs different teaching methods as appropriate (e.g., face-to-face, online, and blended strategies). Committed to enhancing teaching and engaging in scholarly and professional development activities to accommodate changing market needs. Act as liaison between the program and professional organizations through active, individual involvement and, potentially, as the program-appointed representative Enthusiastically support student success through active involvement with individual students, student organizations, and student competitions, both within and outside of the classroom. Remain current in the profession. The position reports to the Department Chair or Director and the Dean. Works independently and collaboratively with effective communication and listening skills. A willingness to work with the Sales and/or Marketing Registered Student Organizations (RSOs). Faculty members also have professional responsibilities, which may include advising students, orientation, and registering students, participation in university committees, keeping regular posted office hours (which are scheduled at times convenient for students), and participation in traditional functions that have academic significance (ex., reporting initial student participation data and submitting final grades on time). Faculty members may be required to teach off-campus or in an online environment. Ferris State University's philosophy places excellence in teaching as the first priority while encouraging scholarly involvement. The candidate will assist in growing and expanding the sales program. Work with colleagues to develop new curricular initiatives. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Cultivate an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: Collegiality and teamwork are essential for this position. The required skills will differ depending on the specific course assignments. For certain undergraduate Sales and Marketing courses, proficiency with tools such as SAP, SPSS, and Google Analytics is required. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcript 1 Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents: Unofficial Transcript 2 Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of their degree. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript. Unofficial Transcript 2 (OPTIONAL): Applicants who have completed college coursework or attained a degree must attach a copy of their unofficial transcript. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript. Initial Application Review Date: November 16, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498287/adjunct-clinical-diagnostic-medical-sonography": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical - Diagnostic Medical Sonography",
      "description": "Adjunct Clinical - Diagnostic Medical Sonography Apply now Job no: 498287 Work type: Faculty - Temporary & Continuing Location: Multiple Locations Categories: Faculty Position Title: Adjunct Clinical - Diagnostic Medical Sonography Location: Multiple Locations Department: 32400 - Diag, Lab & Therapeutic Sciences Advertised Salary: Minimum of $41.73 per hour; the minimum rate increases depending on degree held. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Adjunct Faculty FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Temporary Part-Time/Full-Time: Part-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: As Needed At Will/Just Cause: At Will Summary of Position: The College of Health Professions at Ferris State University seeks a part-time clinical instructor to provide clinical oversight and support to students completing their internship/clinical education experiences at affiliated clinical sites. Adjunct Clinical Instructors serve as liaisons between the student, clinical site, clinical instructor/preceptor, and program to promote student success and ensure appropriate progress toward clinical competencies. Adjunct Clinical Instructors will be responsible for communicating with their assigned clinical sites; performing two visits with the students, one electronically and one in person at the clinical site; reviewing masteries; grading case studies; and documenting progress in Trajecsys. They will be the primary contact for the clinical site, with backup from the 2nd-year clinical coordinator. The anticipated start date of this position is January 2027. However, this is an estimated date and can be revised if needed. Position Type: Faculty - Temporary & Continuing Required Education: Associate degree in Diagnostic Medical Sonography and Bachelor's degree in Diagnostic Medical Sonography, health sciences, education, or related field. Required Work Experience: Two years of clinical sonography experience. Required Licenses and Certifications: ARDMS AB and OB or ARRT (S) current certification. Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Reaching Sitting Twisting Driving Pulling/Pushing Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Master's degree in a health-related field. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Travel to assigned clinical sites and conduct on-site student visits once or twice per semester, or more frequently as needed based on student or clinical site needs. Observe and evaluate student performance in the clinical setting and provide timely feedback regarding strengths, areas for improvement, and overall progress. Guide and support students in applying clinical procedures, skills, and professional practices. Provide students with practical tips, guidance, and recommendations to enhance clinical performance and confidence. Review student progress and documentation in the program’s clinical tracking software, and identify areas requiring additional attention or follow-up. Monitor students' progress toward required clinical competencies and identify skills or areas of mastery that have not yet been demonstrated or achieved. Collaborate with clinical instructors/preceptors to develop strategies for addressing identified performance or competency gaps. Provide constructive coaching and individualized recommendations to help students successfully meet clinical objectives and program requirements. Document site visits, student evaluations, concerns, recommendations, and follow-up activities as appropriate. Communicate significant student concerns or issues to the appropriate program faculty or program coordinator in a timely manner. Maintain professional relationships with clinical affiliates and contribute to positive, collaborative partnerships between the program and clinical sites. Promote adherence to program expectations, clinical site policies, professional standards, and applicable accreditation requirements. Participate in meetings, training, or program activities related to clinical education as requested. Clinical faculty have professional responsibilities in patient care and clinical instruction, which may include being accessible to students outside of regular clinical assignment hours. Participation in traditional functions of academic significance, including assessing students' clinical proficiency in accordance with university systems and guidelines. Clinical faculty are required to provide in-person instruction. Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Certification/License Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of unofficial transcript of appropriate degree per the Required Education Section. Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Finalist will be required to submit an official transcript. Certification (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of ARDMS AB and OB or ARRT (S) current certification. Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498288/dataprocess-analyst-specialist": {
      "title": "Data/Process Analyst Specialist",
      "description": "Data/Process Analyst Specialist Apply now Job no: 498288 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Administrative, Staff Position Title: Data/Process Analyst Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 70201 - Advancement Services Advertised Salary: $65,764.00. See Job Summary for details on salary placement. Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Admin / Admin Temp Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: The Data/Process Analyst Specialist will support technical and functional elements of multiple administrative software applications for the assigned area. This may include daily business operational activities as well as departmental technical activities. This position will support efforts to capture, organize, and analyze constituent data to achieve department and University objectives. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, analyzing current data and system structure; supporting and executing necessary data cleansing and enhancements; implementing efficiency processes; and preserving the accuracy of existing data and the integrity of all constituent records. This position reports directly to the Director of Advancement Services and works closely with the entire University Advancement/Advancement Services staff to understand system user needs. Ongoing responsibilities include addressing the need to remove historical/unwarranted data and/or appropriately archive it before implementing the CRM system. Also working closely with the Prospect Management Analyst, Account Specialist, and Advancement Services Application Specialist. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F1 EAD’s, OPT, H1B, etc. Offers are determined based on a review of the candidate's qualifications, including education, training, experience, and internal pay equity considerations. Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors: Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position. Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role. Final compensation will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Database Management, or 3+ years of related work experience. Required Work Experience: Analyzing system data and reporting information. Experience in higher education. 3+ years’ experience working in data entry, data analysis, and reporting preferred. 3+ years’ experience with Microsoft Office Programs Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge NXT experience preferred. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Reaching Sitting Twisting Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: - Assist and serve as functional backup for application support and account specialist staff. - Review, analyze, and evaluate current systems and user needs. - Provide excellent customer service, be responsive to inquiries, and work to identify and resolve problems. - Lead projects including planning and communications with stakeholders and assign tasks to IT staff if needed. - Work closely with constituents, technical resources, and donor support to troubleshoot end-user processes and reports and collaboratively set project priorities. - Promote teamwork and information sharing within the team, department, and the University. - Create, maintain, and provide documented processes/procedures, projects, and tasks on Advancement Services duties. - Work with donor investment companies to complete any paperwork required to receive donations. - Analyze business process improvements through automation within the departmental application. - Establish and maintain positive interactions with donors, staff, and students. - Maintain the confidentiality of designated information and maintain organizational data in the donor database with consistency and attention to detail. - Assure system integrity and data security. - Troubleshoot problems that arise. - Pull budget reports from CRM to provide to the Director of Advancement Services for Board Reports. - Support the Director of Advancement Services with duties as assigned. - Work with Advisory + of CRM on system issues when needed. - Support all cleanup, enhancement, and accuracy of existing data sources and ensure current constituent data is fresh, current, accurate, and as enhanced as possible to ensure the most effective use of all information available. - Manage projects related to application implementations and integrations. Support data extraction and integration into various systems to enhance operations and decrease errors. - Support all cleanup, enhancement, and accuracy of existing data sources and ensure current constituent data is fresh, current, accurate, and as enhanced as possible to ensure the most effective use of all information available. - Assist with donor impact letters, endowment reports, acknowledgment letters, and other donor literature when needed. - Serve on various University and community committees as assigned. - Create and utilize financial reports to balance CRM to Accounting Banner system for Scholarships awarded through Financial Aid for accuracy. - Process and execute donor Impact Report, which requires working with multiple systems and Financial Aid Leadership staff to satisfy the needs of each donor. - Maintain confidentiality. - Assist with special projects and reports, including responding, as appropriate, to institutional audit requests. -Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. -Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. -Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. -Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. -Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: - Analyze business process improvements. - Evaluate and enhance existing systems. - Input, output, retrieve, and merge information from various software programs and systems. Plan, organize, and make sound judgments and decisions. - Attention to detail, follow-up, and excellent organizational skills independently as well as in a team. - Communicate effectively with staff, IT personnel, and management, both written and verbal communication skills; including demonstrated skill in reading and interpreting documents. - Display a high degree of judgment, discretion, and confidentiality. - Work effectively both independently and as part of a team. - Excellent computer and database skills. - Able to multitask in a demanding, fast-paced environment while under pressure and deadlines. - Flexibility and adaptability to quickly shift focus from one task to another when circumstances require it. - Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498290/rso-greek-life-specialist": {
      "title": "RSO & Greek Life Specialist",
      "description": "RSO & Greek Life Specialist Apply now Job no: 498290 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Administrative, Staff Position Title: RSO & Greek Life Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 62600 - Center for Student Involvement Advertised Salary: $48,232. See Job Summary for details on salary placement. Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Admin / Admin Temp Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: The Center for Student Involvement is seeking applicants for the RSO & Greek Life Specialist in the Center for Student Involvement in the Division of Student Affairs. The RSO & Greek Life Specialist provides support and acts as a resource for all Registered Student Organizations (RSOs) on campus, with special attention to Fraternities and Sororities. This position will advise and support student organizations across campus by providing ongoing training and resources; overseeing their general activities and assisting with event development and management; and providing leadership, accountability, and budget oversight, as well as supporting governing councils and fraternity/sorority chapters. This position will report to the Associate Dean of Student Life. The RSO & Greek Life Specialist maintains a visible presence on campus, must be available to work hours outside the traditional workweek, and is actively engaged in creating and supporting student organization events and traditions. This position is primarily in-person. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Offers are determined based on a review of the candidate's qualifications, including education, training, experience, and internal pay equity considerations. The salary range for this position is aligned with Pay Grade 7. Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors: Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position. Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role. Final compensation will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelor degree from an accredited college or university. Required Work Experience: 1 year of professional or undergraduate experience in Student Affairs, Student Activities, Student Organizations, Fraternity & Sorority Life, campus programming, Residence Life, residence hall programming and/or student leadership. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Carrying Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Experience creating policies, practices, and procedures for Student Organizations and Greek Life. Experience as an executive board member or advisor of a fraternity or sorority. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Develop and maintain quality educational programs for members of student organizations focusing on leadership, risk management, social responsibility, financial responsibility, community service initiatives, and membership recruitment. Mentor and assist students interested in starting a new Registered Student Organization (RSO) throughout the new organization process. Develop and incorporate assessment into programmatic efforts to evaluate progress toward goals related to student learning and engagement. Oversee and coordinate RSO Re-registration and RSO Officer Training. Help current students find RSOs that interest them; this includes coordinating Bulldog Bonanza and Spring RSO Fair. Assist in maintaining, developing, and implementing departmental policies, including the RSO Handbook and the Events and Travel Manual. Serve as a risk manager for student and campus activities and student organizations. Develop and assist with a variety of programming efforts for the Center for Student Involvement and the Division of Student Affairs, including Dawg Days and Admitted Student Open House. Some events take place during the evenings and weekends. Serve as an instrumental liaison between campus and external partners, students, alumni, national offices, and other stakeholders regarding these priorities. Develop and participate in programming hosted through the Center for Student Involvement and Entertainment Unlimited. Collaborate with student organizations, Fraternity & Sorority Life chapters, and advisors to provide guidance, expectations, and support to chapter presidents, officers, alumni, and advisors through regular meetings and communications. Provide support to the University’s four Fraternity & Sorority Life governing councils and maintain a visible presence with each council. Provide program oversight for formal and informal recruitment periods, including marketing and programming efforts to increase awareness of Fraternity & Sorority Life amongst the student body and University community. Coordinate educational and social programs in Fraternity & Sorority Life, such as the New Member Training, Sober Monitor Training, Greek Week, and officer and advisor trainings. Attend monthly All Student Life Meetings. Serve on Committees within Student Affairs and the University. Comply with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA). Serve as a Campus Security Authority and as a Responsible Employee as defined by Clery, Title IX, and Campus Policy. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: Effective communication skills. The ability to manage and complete tasks on time. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript showing their highest degree earned from an accredited college or university. Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Individuals will be required to submit an official transcript prior to hiring. Initial Application Review Date: October 26, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498291/foundation-specialist": {
      "title": "Foundation Specialist",
      "description": "Foundation Specialist Apply now Job no: 498291 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Clerical Position Title: Foundation Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 70000 - Univer Advance and Mktg VP Office Advertised Salary: $25.29 per hour. Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and CTA/MEA-NEA Agreement. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Clerical Tech Association (CTA) FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Clerical-Technical Association (MEA-NEA) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Serves as a key point of contact for the Foundation and Advancement Team and provides administrative support to the Associate Vice President for Advancement/Executive Director of The Ferris Foundation, the Director of Leadership Giving/Associate Director of The Ferris Foundation, and philanthropy officers. Position requires a significant degree of decision-making and independent action. Interacts tactfully and diplomatically with the campus community, vendors, donors, community members, and other University constituents. Position reports to the Associate Vice President for Advancement/Executive Director of The Ferris Foundation. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelor’s degree or work experience equivalent (see below) Satisfactory completion of two years of college or equivalent. The listed requirements represent the knowledge, skills, and/or abilities required. We may consider any equivalent combination of education, training, and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities. Equivalency for education: Two years of full-time, related work experience equals one year of education. Required Work Experience: Three years of relevant leadership experience. Experience with computer software applications, preferably Microsoft Office and a customer/donor database. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Provide responsible, independent administrative support for the Associate Vice President/Executive Director of The Ferris Foundation and the Director of Leadership Giving & Relationships/Associate Director of The Ferris Foundation. Coordinate and manage various office tasks, including budgeting assistance, to ensure smooth department operations. Communicate effectively and promote a positive image of University Advancement and The Ferris Foundation. Coordinate a variety of University Advancement duties that require discretion and/or judgment. Manage executive calendars, including scheduling meetings, appointments, and travel arrangements. Receive information in various forms and determine the appropriate processing method. Provide positive interactions with donors, external and internal constituents, and staff at all levels, operating with courtesy and professionalism. Create, maintain, and update files and recordkeeping systems. Disseminate information that may require explanation and interpretation of established university and departmental policies and procedures, and direct individuals to sources of additional information. Manage multiple, rapidly changing priorities to meet the office's needs. Prepare and process office documents, including purchase orders, contracts/service agreements, and travel requests and expense reports, for the Associate VP for Advancement/Executive Director of The Ferris Foundation and the Director of Leadership Giving/Associate Director of The Ferris Foundation. Independently answers inquiries from a variety of internal and external sources, providing explanation and interpretive information on policies, practices, and procedures. Requests, searches for, retrieves, and analyzes information from a variety of internal and external sources, and compiles it in a usable format. Compiles data and produces materials for presentations and proposals. Composes, drafts, proofreads, and edits correspondence, reports, meeting minutes, and other material. Assists in planning major events/meetings. Serves as the main point of contact for administrative work for the Ferris Foundation Board of Directors. Coordinates correspondence for the Associate Vice President/Executive Director of The Ferris Foundation and the Director of Leadership Giving/Associate Director of Ferris Foundation. Respond to donor inquiries and follow up with appropriate responses. May supervise student workers. Serve as liaison within and outside the University with a variety of constituents. Work with confidential documents and issues. Assist with record-keeping, filing, and archival maintenance. Provide administrative assistance to Philanthropy Officers as needed. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Work some nights and weekends. Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated experience working independently, organizing own work, and coordinating others' work activities. Be exceptionally well-organized and detail-oriented. Be proactive, resourceful, and efficient. Communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Competency with grammar and proofreading skills. Coordinate projects and workflow in an efficient manner Be tactful and courteous at all times. Successfully interact with a diverse range of students, faculty, staff, alumni, donors, and visitors in various situations. Plan, organize, and make sound judgments and decisions. Perform relevant research. Work cooperatively in a fast-paced, demanding atmosphere. Respond appropriately, efficiently, and positively to direction from supervisors and others. Perform complex computer operations using a variety of software applications. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Unofficial Transcript 2 Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498292/secretary-level-2": {
      "title": "Secretary Level 2",
      "description": "Secretary Level 2 Apply now Job no: 498292 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Clerical Position Title: Secretary Level 2 Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 31100 - Charter Schools Advertised Salary: $18.45; Hourly rate pursuant to FSU & CTA/MEA-NEA Agreement. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Clerical Tech Association (CTA) FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Clerical-Technical Association (MEA-NEA) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Seeking qualified applicants to provide responsible, independent secretarial support in accordance with established departmental policies and procedures. This position is located in the Charter Schools Office (CSO) on the Big Rapids campus and is a CTA/MEA-NEA bargaining unit position. The anticipated start date for this position is November 2026. However, this is an estimated date and can be revised if needed. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Satisfactory completion of two years of college or equivalent. The listed requirements represent the required knowledge, skills, and/or abilities. Any equivalent combination of education, training, and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities may be considered. Equivalency for education: Two years of full-time, related work experience equals one year of education. Required Work Experience: Two years of full-time secretarial work experience, including public contact where tact and diplomacy are required. Proficient in data entry and accurate typing skills; proficient in Microsoft Office 365, especially Microsoft Word and Excel. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Independently answer routine correspondence. Draft non-routine correspondence for the supervisor's review and approval. Research information to support incoming and outgoing communications. Prepare and maintain information for documents such as correspondence, memos, and reports, using software for word processing, spreadsheets, databases, and file management. Input, retrieve, download, and output information utilizing a computer to access various software programs and systems. Answer or refer inquiries from academy staff and the general public regarding established policies and procedures. Support the Director and Associate Director. Perform bookkeeping/recordkeeping/calculations for such things as employee assignments, Departmental budget expenditures, encumbrances, balances, reconciliations, and deposits. Plan, process, and monitor staff travel expenses and the travel budget, including using Concur. Establish and maintain filing and recordkeeping systems. Perform any/all duties as defined in the Secretary, Level 1 position description. Interview, recommend for hire, train, and direct student employees. Coordinate special departmental functions, such as meetings, conferences, workshops, and seminars, by scheduling facilities, preparing agendas, and arranging services and equipment. Maintain the confidentiality of designated information. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Provide back-up assistance for other clerical positions and perform routine office support duties. Attend meetings and conferences in the supervisor's absence. Skills and Abilities: Communicate effectively in a variety of situations. Input, retrieve, download, merge, and output information from software programs and systems. Operate a variety of office equipment, such as computers, multi-line telephones, and copiers. Perform basic mathematical operations with accuracy. Plan, organize, and make sound judgments and decisions. Use computer software such as word processing, spreadsheets, and databases. Utilize the rules of proper grammar, correct spelling and punctuation, and correct arrangement of information. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Unofficial Transcript 2 Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants are required to provide a brief cover letter and a resume. Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of their two years of college. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. The individual hired will be required to submit an official transcript. If you do not have a college transcript that meets the required education listed, please write a justification explaining how your work experience is equivalent to the required education and attach that justification in lieu of the transcript. Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498293/administrative-specialist": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist Apply now Job no: 498293 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Clerical Position Title: Administrative Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 34000 - COB Deans Office Advertised Salary: $23.43; Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and CTA/MEA-NEA Agreement. Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Clerical Tech Association (CTA) FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: The College of Business at Ferris State University is seeking an Administrative Specialist. Working under the general direction of an administrator, use independent judgment to perform a variety of administrative duties. Primary responsibilities will include: supporting student services, including serving as a point of contact and assisting the Office of Student Academic Affairs, and maintaining the student services webpage. Provide support to the Dean's Office as needed during clerical or administrative staff absences. As part of the College of Business, you will join a team committed to experiential learning, strong industry partnerships, and student success. This role offers the opportunity to support innovative programs, build meaningful connections with students and community partners, and help shape the next generation of Bulldog graduates. The Administrative Specialist is responsible for coordinating student recruitment and engagement initiatives for the College of Business. The successful candidate will implement recruitment strategies that support the college's mission, vision, and enrollment goals. The anticipated start date for this position is November 2026. However, this is an estimated date and can be revised if needed. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skills, and/or abilities required. Any equivalent combination of education, training, and experience that provides the required knowledge, skills, and abilities may be considered. Equivalency for education is two years of full-time related work experience, which equals one year of education. Required Work Experience: Proficiency with computer applications such as Microsoft Office suite, Adobe, and other word-processing, LMS, and visual graphics platforms. Demonstrate sustained accomplishments in event coordination, independent decision-making, and the implementation of policies and procedures. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Bending Carrying Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Office experience, including high-level customer service. Experience assisting with project or event management. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Serve as a liaison between college stakeholders (e.g., students, prospective students, and registered student organizations). Prepare, or assist in preparing, special projects. Regularly deal with sensitive and confidential matters. Including assisting in situations involving sensitive issues or decision-making otherwise handled by the supervisor. Participate in planning and executing recruitment activities. Maintain current knowledge of pertinent regulations, compliance issues, and university policies applicable to the specific area of assignment. Independently answer inquiries from a variety of internal and external sources. Work directly with students to provide support services and resources. Maintaining the confidentiality of designated information in accordance with FERPA, HIPAA, and other applicable standards. Assist with maintaining the College's website pages. Interview, recommend for hire, and supervise student employees Collect, organize, and prepare data for internal reporting, state compliance, accreditation reviews, and key performance indicators. Assist with the planning and execution of events such as orientations, welcome back week, homecoming, and award ceremonies. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Participate in university committees, task forces, and working groups as assigned. Attend professional development workshops, training sessions, and conferences relevant to dual enrollment, transfer, and administrative operations. Contribute to process improvement initiatives within the unit and division. Skills and Abilities: Communicate effectively and professionally with a variety of customer population. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Demonstrate project management skills. Plan, organize, and make sound judgments and decisions. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of a bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university. The transcript must include the institution name, applicant name, date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. The individual hired will be required to submit an official transcript. If you do not have a college transcript that meets the required education listed, please write a justification explaining how your work experience is equivalent to the required education, and attach it in lieu of the transcript. Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498295/visitor-services-assistant": {
      "title": "Visitor Services Assistant",
      "description": "Visitor Services Assistant Apply now Job no: 498295 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Part-Time Position Title: Visitor Services Assistant Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 95200 - Jim Crow Museum Advertised Salary: $20.00 per hour Benefits: Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Part Time Support FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Temporary Part-Time/Full-Time: Part-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: At Will Summary of Position: The Visitor Services Assistant provides front-line visitor services and operational support for the Jim Crow Museum. This position helps create a welcoming, respectful, organized, and educational experience for all museum visitors from arrival through departure. Primary responsibilities include greeting and orienting visitors, assisting with admissions and ticketing, responding to visitor questions, providing information about museum policies and exhibits, supporting group arrivals and special events, monitoring public spaces, and assisting with the museum's daily operations. This isa part-time position limited to no more than 28 hours per week. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High School diploma Required Work Experience: Experience working with the public in a customer service, hospitality, retail, educational, museum, or similar environment. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Moving Sitting Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Welcome visitors and serve as a primary point of contact at the Jim Crow Museum. • Provide visitors with information about admission, museum hours, exhibits, amenities, accessibility, policies, programs, and special events. • Assist visitors with ticket purchases, check-in, reservations, and other admission-related processes. • Work with student employees to ensure front-of-house operations are covered. • Respond professionally and appropriately to visitor questions and concerns. • Monitor galleries and other public spaces to support visitor safety, appropriate conduct, and protection of museum objects and exhibits. • Maintain an orderly and professional guest services/front desk area. • Answer telephone inquiries and assist with general museum correspondence as assigned. • Assist with museum retail or gift shop operations, including sales and basic point-of-sale functions, as assigned. • Assist with opening and closing procedures. • Communicate visitor concerns, facility issues, emergencies, or unusual incidents promptly to appropriate museum staff. • Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. • Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. • Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. • Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: • Effective verbal communication skills and ability to communicate with individuals and groups. • Ability to interact respectfully and professionally with visitors of diverse ages, backgrounds, identities, and perspectives. • Ability to learn and accurately communicate museum information, policies, and procedures. • Ability to exercise appropriate judgment regarding when a visitor concern should be referred to supervisory or professional museum staff. • Dependability and ability to work independently as well as part of a team. • Ability to maintain confidentiality of designated information and perform duties in accordance with applicable University and museum policies and procedures. • Basic computer skills and ability to learn ticketing, point-of-sale, reservation, and other museum systems. • Ability to work Saturdays and weekday evenings when necessary. • Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498296/menswomens-assistant-tennis-coach": {
      "title": "Men's/Women's Assistant Tennis Coach",
      "description": "Men's/Women's Assistant Tennis Coach Apply now Job no: 498296 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Part-Time Position Title: Men's/Women's Assistant Tennis Coach Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 51600 - Gen Athletics Advertised Salary: $15.00 Benefits: Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Part Time Support FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Temporary Part-Time/Full-Time: Part-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 9 Month At Will/Just Cause: At Will Summary of Position: The Assistant Tennis Coach will assist the head coach with all aspects of planning, organizing and supervising a highly competitive NCAA Division II Men's and Women's Tennis program. A successful candidate will demonstrate a strong work ethic and energy. Also, must be committed to the Ferris State University Athletic Department's vision and core values of collaboration, diversity, ethical community, excellence, learning, and opportunity. This is a nine-month position from September 1st to May 30th that will work approximately 22 hours a week @ $15.00 an hour. This is a part time position and may not work more than 28 hours per week. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelors Degree Required Work Experience: At least two years of intercollegiate playing experience, or coaching collegiate tennis or high school tennis. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Assist Head Coach in recruitment of qualified student athletes. Coordinate on-campus recruiting visits. Assist Head Coach in organizing, planning, programming and help run camps and clinics for recruitment purposes. Assist with on-court coaching and match preparation. Monitor the physical and academic development of both men's and women's tennis student- athletes. Assist in coordinating and running practices in compliance with NCAA rules and regulations. Mentor student-athletes and monitor their overall mental health. Assist with fundraising efforts. Assist in preparing travel and game itineraries. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of unofficial transcript of a Bachelors degree from an accredited college or university. Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Finalist will be required to submit an official transcript. Initial Application Review Date: October 19, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498298/food-service-worker": {
      "title": "Food Service Worker",
      "description": "Food Service Worker Apply now Job no: 498298 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Food Service Worker Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 51803 - Quad Cafe Advertised Salary: $17.53 hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement. Benefits: Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: • A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at the Quad Café. The normal working hours are Monday, 1:30pm-10pm and Tuesday through Friday 12:30 p.m. to 9 p.m., . Days off are Saturday and Sunday. • The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. • Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. • If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. • Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. • This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position. Position Type: Staff Required Education: • High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: • Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial or institutional food service to include food preparation. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Train others in the performance of the characteristic duties as directed. • Assist other food service employees as needed. • Assure that food is palatable and appetizing. • Cook and handle food according to safe food handling/sanitary requirements, following departmental sanitation policies. • Interact with customers and staff in a polite, friendly, and courteous manner. • Maintain equipment, pots, pans, utensils, and work area in a clean, orderly, and sanitary condition following departmental sanitation policies. • Minimize food waste. • Obtain foods from storage areas. • Operate various kitchen equipment and machines and utilize utensils. • Perform the work of other Dining Service classifications when assigned. • Prepare food for serving and ensure continued food availability. • Support, promote, and develop University student enrollment and retention initiatives. • Demonstrates an understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion, especially in working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and community members. • Prepare foods using recipes generated from the computerized menu management system. • Respond to special dietary requests. • Set up and maintain food preparation area, food serving, and display areas in an attractive and sanitary manner. • Maintain safety and sanitation standards in all duties and responsibilities. • Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. • Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. • Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. • Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. • Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: • Remove trash, break down cardboard boxes, and assist in the University's recycling efforts. Skills and Abilities: • Ability to communicate effectively. • Ability to interact with the public in a friendly, polite, and courteous manner. • Be familiar with seasoning requirements and kitchen equipment. • Cook a variety of foods in large and small quantities. • Follow safety and sanitation standards and practices. • Keep accurate records. • Read, understand and follow recipes, directions, safety labels, equipment operation manuals, etc. • Work harmoniously with others in variable temperatures, in close confines, noise, and stressful situations and workloads. • Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications listed in the job posting to be considered for the position. Initial Application Review Date: October 16, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498300/custodian": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian Apply now Job no: 498300 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Custodian Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55200 - Bldg Custodial Admin Advertised Salary: $17.88 per hour. Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. This is a custodial position, S-Th, 10:30 pm - 7:00 am. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: Custodial/Janitorial work experience in a commercial, hospital, or school environment, in a commercial cleaning service, or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training. Demonstrated experience in the proper operation of a variety of commercial custodial equipment, such as vacuum cleaners, automatic scrubbers, high-speed burnishers, single-disc scrubbers, carpet extraction/shampoo equipment, and other essential or similar custodial equipment. Required Licenses and Certifications: Valid driver’s license. Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Electrical Hazards Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Twisting Climbing Driving Heights Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Any other related custodial experience. Please include any/all related work experience associated with the required qualifications for this position. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Change linens, make beds, and bunk/debunk beds. Check fire extinguishers and related equipment as scheduled, and report any deficiencies to the supervisor. Depending on the assignment, may be required to move custodial equipment, fill in for vacant positions, etc. Disinfect restrooms, showers, and locker rooms. Empty waste baskets and trash containers, and gather and dispose of trash and foreign material from the assigned area (to include the perimeter of the assigned building) Maintain current knowledge of bloodborne pathogens policies and procedures. May be responsible for carrying, distributing, and delivering custodial supplies and equipment. Minimize waste of cleaning supplies, paper, soap, and other supplies. Open and close buildings, classrooms, offices, and other facilities in assigned areas. Remove snow and ice from entrances of assigned areas; apply salt as necessary. Replace light bulbs, globes, tubes, and light lenses. Replenish paper and soap products. Report needed maintenance on assigned equipment. Report needed repairs to the supervisor, or call the physical plant in an emergency. Respond to emergency custodial requests (which may include blood and bodily fluid cleanup). Set up tables, chairs, and other related furniture as needed. Sweep, wet-mop, refinish hard-surface floors, clean carpet, and vacuum. Use a household plunger to unclog commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture. Wash walls, woodwork, windows, blinds, mirrors, bathroom fixtures, furniture, chalk/white boards, and climb ladders. Work with various cleaning chemicals and equipment, follow procedures for safe handling and use, and wear assigned protective equipment. Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Assist other service workers as needed. Train and direct others in performing the characteristic duties. Carry out these responsibilities in accordance with University policies and applicable laws. Maintain the safety and security of equipment, the safe operation of vehicles, and the security of keys, tools, materials, and inventories. Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities. Report to immediate supervisor. Skills and Abilities: Communicate and work effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors. Exercise good judgment in resolving situations related to cleaning and proper chemical use, referring unusual problems to the supervisor. Maintain a high standard of cleanliness and follow safety and disinfecting standards and practices. Read, understand, and follow instructions, safety and direction labels, and equipment operation manuals. Train and direct others in performing the characteristic duties. Work harmoniously with and lead others in all situations, including environments with variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads. Work independently. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position. Initial Application Review Date: October 16, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
