    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498306/electrician": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Electrician Apply now Job no: 498306 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Electrician Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55501 - Electrical Advertised Salary: $30.91. hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Perform skilled trades work in installing, inspecting, maintaining, diagnosing, and/or wiring electrical equipment and devices of any voltage as required to maintain the function and operation of the University. This is an electrician position that will normally work M-F, 8:00 am – 4:30 pm. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: No Minimum years of experience required other than the requirement to obtain a Journeyman electrical license. Required Licenses and Certifications: Valid driver’s license. State of Michigan Journeyman Electrical License. Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Electrical Hazards Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Climbing Driving Heights Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Master Electrician license. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Estimate material requirements for assigned work. Install, inspect, maintain, diagnose, and repair all electrical wiring, equipment, and apparatus used for all signaling systems and circuits, such as fire alarms, security alarms, time systems, bell systems, etc., as allowed by law. (Telephone communications systems excluded.) Install, inspect, maintain, diagnose, and repair all electrical wiring, equipment, and apparatus used for the distribution and utilization of electrical energy for power and lighting in both permanent and temporary circuits and systems at the required voltage. Install, inspect, maintain, diagnose, and repair all electrical wiring, equipment, and apparatus used for the production, distribution, and utilization of electrical energy for all emergency and standby systems and circuits. Maintain assigned tools and keep equipment and mechanical space in a neat, organized, and clean, non-hazardous environment. May be required to secure the required electrical permits. Prepare records and reports as assigned. Provide emergency shutdown and passenger evacuation from all elevators as provided by law. Stock, maintain, and operate a service vehicle in a neat, organized, and safe manner. Maintain the safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories. Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities. Report to immediate supervisor. Train and oversee the work of other employees in performing the characteristic duties. Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Assist in or perform work on other mechanical systems as needed. Skills and Abilities: Communicate effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors. Demonstrate the ability to climb a 100’ light pole. Direct and train others in performing the characteristic duties. Erect and work from ladders, scaffolds, elevated work platforms, light poles, bucket trucks, etc. Keep and maintain accurate records. Maintain University standards of good workmanship in both quality and quantity. Perform mathematical computations with a high degree of accuracy. Perform skilled work in all electrical-related duties. Read, understand, interpret, and follow blueprints, sketches, schematics, specifications, directions, safety labels, and equipment operation manuals. Understand and know methods, codes, regulations, materials, tools, equipment, occupational hazards, and safety precautions of the electrical trade. Understand, use good judgment, and follow procedures established through safety training and the physical plant safety manual. Work harmoniously with and direct others in situations involving variable temperatures, occasional noise, stressful workloads, and inclement weather. Work independently. Work with the least amount of inconvenience to all people involved. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Certification/License Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants need to ensure that their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications that are posted on the job posting in order to be considered for the position. Initial Application Review Date: October 16, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498308/grounds-specialist": {
      "title": "Grounds Specialist",
      "description": "Grounds Specialist Apply now Job no: 498308 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Grounds Specialist Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55100 - Grounds Advertised Salary: $ 22.38. Pursuant to the AFSCME collective bargaining agreement Benefits: Comprehensive benefits package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Perform independent maintenance and repair of campus grounds, roads, walks, plant life, irrigation systems, and grounds equipment using approved environmental and ecological practices. May require availability to work other shifts, weekends, and evenings, including overtime and emergency call-outs. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University requirements concerning the issuance and use of University keys. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: Three years full-time equivalent landscape maintenance and landscape construction including all elements of flat concrete work. One season of commercial licensed pesticide application. Landscape design education or experience. Required Licenses and Certifications: Valid (current) State of Michigan Pesticide Application License – Category 3a, 3b. Must become qualified in Category 5 Aquatics within six months of hire. Successful applicant will be required to complete a three month landscape design course at eCornell within 9 months from date of hire. Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Balancing Climbing Driving Lifting Pulling/Pushing Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Calculate pesticide application methods and calibrations. Use and follow pesticide safety guidelines as dictated by state and federal regulations and FSU-established criteria. Install and maintain irrigation systems. Install and perform finished concrete flatwork; repair concrete flatwork. Maintain campus lawns and all plant life, including flower and shrub beds, including but not limited to planting, mowing, shoveling, leaf and litter removal, mulching, sweeping, etc. Mix and/or apply pesticides (State of Michigan license required), adjuvants, and related products, as well as general ready-to-use, non-licensing-required pesticides and related products. Pruning of trees, shrubs, and other plant life. Snow and ice removal from campus roads, lots, walks, steps, ramps, etc., with demonstrated ability to operate the necessary equipment. Other duties may be assigned. Maintain the safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories. Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities. Report to immediate supervisor. Coordinate between spray applicators and the supervisor and maintain spray inventory. Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Responsible for maintaining confidentiality of information pursuant to university policies and/or state or federal laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Assist in the repair and installation of landscape fencing. Assist other grounds employees as needed. Train students and employees in performing the characteristic duties; direct students’ work. Maintain and perform minor repairs to grounds maintenance equipment (e.g., blade replacement, sharpening, greasing). Request necessary service, garage maintenance, and/or repair of grounds maintenance equipment. Install, maintain, and repair storm drain systems and/or subsurface water control (footers, drains, etc.). Survey site elevations and distances for various landscape and grounds maintenance functions and projects. Maintain sports turf and playing surfaces, including field layout and paint striping. Repair and maintain roads and parking lots, and install and maintain sidewalks, bollards, signs, etc. Construct and/or install landscape functions such as hardscape construction (e.g., modular and/or retaining walls, paver bricks, patios, walkways, benches, etc.). Skills and Abilities: Be familiar with identifying trees, shrubs, perennials, and annuals. Communicate effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors. Demonstrated knowledge of accepted A.A.N. (American Association of Nurserymen) methods of pruning trees and shrubs. Familiarity with and proficiency in the safe and efficient operation and maintenance of small-engine and grounds equipment, such as light-duty trucks, small engines, lawn mowers, light-duty tractors and trucks, snow removal machines, air compressors, and other machinery. Maintain University and grounds maintenance industry standards of good workmanship in both quality and quantity. Perform duties of higher and lower grounds classifications. Read, understand, interpret, and follow directions, blueprints, safety labels, and equipment operation manuals. Skills and abilities to perform essential and marginal duties. Train and direct students and employees in performing the characteristic duties. Understand, use good judgment, and follow procedures established through safety training and the Physical Plant Safety Manual. Work independently. Work with and lead others in situations involving variable temperatures, noise, stressful workloads, and inclement weather. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Certification/License Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: AFSCME members need to ensure their application reflects that minimum requirements have been met in order to be considered for the position. Initial Application Review Date: October 16, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498309/construction-lab-asttutor-student-position": {
      "title": "Construction Lab Ast/Tutor (Student Position)",
      "description": "Construction Lab Ast/Tutor (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498309 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Construction Mgmt Computer Lab Assistant/Tutor (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: Construction Advertised Salary: $14.00-$14.49 Summary of Position: Construction Lab Assistants assist the professor with miscellaneous duties such as inventory of tools, distribution and collection of tools and supplies to students, setting up lab equipment, lead clean-up, and assist students with lab operations Position Requirements: - Construction Technology & Management Program student (BCTM, CETH, CONM) sophomore level or higher - Successful completion of CONM 111 Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Support of lab operations as required Assist CTMG faculty in necessary functions during lab periods such as setting up, leading clean-up, troubleshooting equipment, operating overhead crane, assisting CTMG students with lab operations (sequencing, methods, materials, tolerances, and standards). Other duties as assigned Number of Positions Available: 4 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
