    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498221/custodian": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian Apply now Job no: 498221 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Custodian Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55200 - Bldg Custodial Admin Advertised Salary: $17.88 - hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement Benefits: Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. This is a custodial position, M-F, 5:00 pm - 1:30 am. Position Type: Staff Required Education: High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: Custodial/Janitorial work experience in a commercial-hospital-school environment, in a commercial cleaning service, or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training. Demonstrated experience with the correct operation of a variety of commercial custodial equipment, such as vacuum cleaners, automatic scrubbers, high-speed burnishers, single-disc scrubbers, carpet extraction/shampoo equipment, or other essential or similar custodial equipment. Required Licenses and Certifications: Valid driver’s license. Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Electrical Hazards Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Twisting Climbing Driving Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Any other related custodial experience. Please include any/all related work experience associated with the required qualifications for this position. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Change linens, make beds, and bunk/debunk beds. Check fire extinguishers and related equipment as scheduled, and report any deficiencies to the supervisor. Depending on the assignment, you may be required to move custodial equipment, fill in for vacant positions, etc. Disinfect restrooms, showers, and locker rooms. Empty waste baskets and trash containers, and gather and dispose of trash and foreign material from the assigned area (to include the perimeter of the assigned building) Maintain current knowledge of bloodborne pathogens policies and procedures. May be responsible for carrying, distributing, and delivering custodial supplies and equipment. Minimize waste of cleaning, paper, soap, and other supplies. Open and close buildings, classrooms, offices, and similar spaces in the assigned areas. Remove snow and ice from entrances of assigned areas, apply salt as necessary. Replace light bulbs, globes, tubes, and light lenses. Replenish paper and soap products. Report needed maintenance on assigned equipment. Report needed repairs to the supervisor or call the physical plant in emergencies. Respond to emergency custodial requests (which could include blood and body fluid clean-up). Set up tables, chairs, and other related furniture as needed. Sweep, wet mop, refinish hard surface floors, clean carpet, vacuum. Utilize a household plunger to unplug commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture. Wash walls, woodwork, windows, blinds, mirrors, bathroom fixtures, furniture, chalk/white boards, and climb ladders. Work with various cleaning chemicals and equipment, follow procedures for safe handling and use, and wear assigned protective equipment. Maintain the safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories. Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities. Report to the immediate supervisor. Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Assist other service workers as needed. Train and direct others in the performance of the characteristic duties. Carry out these responsibilities in accordance with University policies and applicable laws. Skills and Abilities: Communicate and work effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors. Exercise good judgment in resolving situations related to cleaning and proper chemical use, referring unusual problems to a supervisor. Maintain a high standard of cleanliness and follow safety and disinfecting standards and practices. Read, understand, and follow instructions, safety and direction labels, and equipment operation manuals. Train and direct others in the performance of the characteristic duties. Work harmoniously with and lead others in all situations, including those environments that may involve variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads. Work independently. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position. Initial Application Review Date: September 28, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498222/kendall-graphic-design-assist-student-position": {
      "title": "Kendall- Graphic Design Assist (Student Position)",
      "description": "Kendall- Graphic Design Assist (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498222 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: KCAD Graphic Design Assistant (Student Position) Location: Grand Rapids, MI Department: Kendall College of Art and Design Advertised Salary: $13.99 Summary of Position: The Graphic Design intern will assist the Dean’s Office in creating, implementing, and maintaining physical and digital graphic assets that support the recruitment and retention of KCAD students. In addition, this position will work with the Dean’s Office to put together assets for KCAD’s social media platforms. The position offers up to 10 hours/week. The weekly schedule will be determined by the student's availability and the Dean’s Office’s needs. Hours are flexible and can be adjusted to fit the student's course schedule as it changes from semester to semester. Position Requirements: Proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop). Familiarity with Canva and Microsoft Office. Basic knowledge of typography, layout, color theory, and branding principles. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Ability to work independently while also contributing as part of a collaborative team. Excellent time management and communication skills. A willingness to try new things and learn on the job. Photography or videography experience is a plus. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Graphic Design & Creative Development Design print and digital marketing materials, including flyers, posters, brochures, postcards, and banners. Create graphics for social media campaigns, websites, email communications, and digital signage. Assist in developing visual assets for student recruitment and admissions initiatives. Create branded templates for internal college communications and presentations. Prepare production-ready files for print and digital distribution. Design promotional materials for exhibitions, lectures, orientations, portfolio reviews, open houses, and other college events. Assist with environmental graphics and signage for campus events. Branding & Marketing Ensure all creative materials align with KCAD and Ferris State University brand standards. Participate in brainstorming sessions for marketing campaigns and event promotions. Research current design trends and recommend creative ideas to enhance marketing efforts. Help develop visual concepts that showcase student success, academic programs, and campus life. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Photography & Multimedia Photograph campus events, student work, and college activities. Provide on-site creative support during major campus events when needed. Edit and retouch photos for marketing and promotional use. Assist with basic video editing and motion graphics for social media and promotional videos. Organize and maintain the college's digital photo and design asset library. Number of Positions Available: 3 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498224/custodian-9month": {
      "title": "Custodian (9-Month)",
      "description": "Custodian (9-Month) Apply now Job no: 498224 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Staff, Service/Maintenance Position Title: Custodian (9-Month) Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 55200 - Bldg Custodial Admin Advertised Salary: $17.88- hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement Benefits: Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. AFSCME Benefits FLSA: Non-Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609) Term of Position: 9 Month At Will/Just Cause: Just Cause Summary of Position: • Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. • This is a 9-month custodial position, M-F, 5:00 pm – 1:30 am. • All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position. Position Type: Staff Required Education: • High school diploma or GED equivalency. Required Work Experience: • Custodial/Janitorial work experience in a commercial-hospital-school environment, in a commercial cleaning service, or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training. • Demonstrated experience with correct operation of a variety of commercial custodial equipment such as vacuum cleaner, automatic scrubber, high speed burnisher, single disc scrubber, carpet extraction/shampoo equipment or other essential or similar custodial equipment. Required Licenses and Certifications: • Valid driver’s license. Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Electrical Hazards Inclement Weather Moving Reaching Twisting Balancing Climbing Driving Heights Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: • Any other related custodial experience. Please include any/all related work experience associated with the required qualifications for this position. • Demonstrates an understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion, especially in working relationships with students, faculty, staff and community members. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Change linens, make beds, and bunk/debunk beds. • Check fire extinguishers and related equipment as scheduled; report any deficiencies to supervisor. • Depending on assignment, may be required to move custodial equipment, fill in for vacant positions, etc. • Disinfect restrooms, showers, and locker rooms. • Empty waste baskets and trash containers and gather and dispose of trash and foreign material from assigned area (to include perimeter of assigned building) • Maintain current knowledge of bloodborne pathogens policies and procedures. • May be responsible for carrying, distributing, and delivering custodial supplies and equipment. • Minimize waste of cleaning, paper, soap, and other supplies. • Open and close buildings, classrooms, offices, etc. of assigned areas. • Remove snow and ice from entrances of assigned areas, apply salt as necessary. • Replace light bulbs, globes, tubes, and light lenses. • Replenish paper and soap products. • Report needed maintenance on assigned equipment. • Report needed repairs to supervisor or call physical plant in emergencies. • Respond to emergency custodial requests (which could include blood and body fluid clean-up). • Set up tables, chairs, and other related furniture as needed. • Sweep, wet mop, refinish hard surface floors, clean carpet, vacuum. • Utilize a household plunger to unplug commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture. • Wash walls, woodwork, windows, blinds, mirrors, bathroom fixtures, furniture, chalk/white boards, and climb ladders. • Work with different cleaning chemicals and equipment and follow procedures for safe handling and use, and wear assigned protective equipment. • Maintain safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories. • Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities. • Report to immediate supervisor. • Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. • Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. • Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. • Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. • Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: • Assist other service workers as needed. • Carry out these responsibilities in accordance with University policies and applicable laws. Skills and Abilities: • Communicate and work effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors. • Exercise good judgment in resolving situations related to cleaning and proper chemical use, referring unusual problems to the supervisor. • Maintain a high standard of cleanliness and follow safety and disinfecting standards and practices. • Experience working directly with people from diverse racial, ethnic, and socioeconomic backgrounds. • Read, understand, and follow instructions, safety and direction labels, equipment operations manuals, etc. • Train and guide others in the performance of the characteristic duties. • Work harmoniously with and guide others in all situations, including those environments which may involve variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads. • Work independently. • Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position. Initial Application Review Date: September 28, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498225/assistant-dean-of-student-success": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean of Student Success",
      "description": "Assistant Dean of Student Success Apply now Job no: 498225 Work type: Staff Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Administrative, Staff Position Title: Assistant Dean of Student Success Location: Big Rapids (Main Campus) Department: 37000 - Pharmacy Deans Office Advertised Salary: $131,462; See Job Summary for details on salary placement. Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements. Benefits: Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Admin/Admin Temp Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 12 Month At Will/Just Cause: At Will Summary of Position: The Assistant Dean of Student Success (ADSS) directs and coordinates the College's Office of Student Success and provides leadership to ensure compliance with all accreditation standards related to student services. Specific responsibilities related to student success include overseeing recruitment, admissions, student advising, and development and analysis of key metrics that assess student success, well-being, and belonging. The ADSS will provide leadership in planning key student experiences such as orientation, career fairs, and ceremonial events (e.g., White Coat Ceremony, Doctoral Hooding Ceremony). In addition, the position is expected to foster a collaborative work environment with College and University faculty, staff, and administration, as well as College committees. Limited instructional responsibilities as determined to be appropriate based on expertise and academic background. Pursuit of research/scholarly activities is encouraged. The anticipated start date of this position is January 2027; however, this is an estimated date and can be revised if needed. Offers are determined based on a review of the candidate's qualifications, including education, training, experience, and internal pay equity considerations. Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors: - Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position. - Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role. - Upper Range: Candidates with seven or more years of directly related experience, advanced knowledge, specialized skills, certifications, or expertise that provide significant value to the position. Final compensation will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F1 EAD’s, OPT, H1B, etc. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Terminal degree (Ph.D., Pharm.D., Ed.D.) in higher education, student services, educational administration, pharmacy, or related field. Required Work Experience: Five or more years of experience in higher education that includes teaching (didactic or experiential), academic advising and/or academic program administration. Extensive experience in presenting to diverse audiences. Demonstratable commitment to student well-being. Understanding of professional/doctoral programming and healthcare education. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Office Environment Carrying Lifting Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Terminal degree in a healthcare-related or higher education field. Ability to effectively utilize technology and academic, admissions, and assessment databases. Experience in higher education student services in pharmacy, medicine, or related field. Experience in advising/working with pharmacy or pre-pharmacy students in advising activities and career exploration. Knowledgeable of various pedagogical methods currently employed in higher education. Capable of designing research protocols in academic settings. Experience in policy creation and implementation. Demonstrated excellent written and verbal communication skills. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Oversee recruitment, orientation, retention, and progression programs/initiatives within the college. Serve as the direct report for the Office of Student Success, recruitment and admissions staff, and office support staff. Serve as a member of the College's Admissions Committee, Progressions Committee, and Executive Council. Collaborate with the Assistant Dean of Academics and Admissions (ADAA) to support student academic progression, remediation, and retention efforts. Work directly with students and serve in an advisory role. Oversee compliance with all Federal Equal Opportunity and Americans with Disability Act policies within the College and work directly with the University Office of Educational Counseling and Disability Services. Serve as a liaison between the College and the University's Office of the Vice-President for Student Affairs. Oversee student academic, professional, and career success, ensuring that all students gain access to the highest quality faculty advising, career coaching, disabilities, tutoring, and counseling resources as appropriate. Ensure students are orientated to the mission, goals, values, and educational philosophy or the College. Provide required data for reporting to external organizations (e.g. AACP, ACPE). Monitor compliance with codes of professional conduct, honor codes, and professional behavior expectations. Ensure due process for all parties in cases of academic and non-academic misconduct. Maintain an official complaint log as required by accreditation standards and report regularly to the Executive Council regarding student complaints. Oversee/assure consistent student services for both campus locations and for students on experiential placements. Align budgets and human resources to support student academic success. Represent the college at assigned conferences, meetings, and professional organizations. Ensure proper oversight of all registered student organizations (RSO) and compliance with pertinent standards. Collaborate with the Accreditation and Continuous Quality Improvement Committee to develop and interpret relevant metrics to guide quality improvements in student services. Responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of designated information. Perform all duties in compliance with applicable University policies and procedures and state and federal requirements. Supervise Office of Student Success staff members. Report directly to the Dean of the College of Pharmacy. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Travel as needed, including overnight and weekend assignments. Other duties, as assigned. Skills and Abilities: Effectively communicate complex topics in an organized and effective manner. Develop and implement effective policies and procedures. Work effectively with diverse groups, including faculty, students, parents, and alumni. Recognize problems, develop effective solutions, and maintain a high level of accuracy. Effectively manage projects and processes to achieve administrative efficiencies. Analyze trends and appropriately communicate observations to colleagues. Lead the development, implementation, and assessment of an effective vision for the Office of Student Success. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcript 1 Other Additional Document Optional Documents: Philosophy of supporting student success in a professional academic program. Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of unofficial transcript of terminal degree. Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Finalist will be required to submit an official transcript. Other Additional Document (REQUIRED): Philosophy of supporting student success in a professional academic program. Initial Application Review Date: October 12, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498226/woodshop-specialist": {
      "title": "Woodshop Specialist",
      "description": "Woodshop Specialist Apply now Job no: 498226 Work type: Staff Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Administrative, Staff Position Title: Woodshop Specialist Location: Grand Rapids (Kendall) Department: 45025 - KCAD Model Shop Lab Advertised Salary: $35,209; See Job Summary for details on salary placement Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements. Benefits: Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position. Admin/Admin Temp Benefit Plans FLSA: Exempt Temporary/Continuing: Continuing Part-Time/Full-Time: Full-Time Union Group: N/A Term of Position: 9 Month At Will/Just Cause: At Will Summary of Position: To maintain a well-equipped, easily accessible multimedia shop facility with the purpose of promoting a safe, barrier-free, creative learning environment for faculty, staff, and students. The work year for this position is 1 week before students start in August and 1 week after exams in the spring. The calendar calculation is 190 days in 26-27 or .73 The anticipated start date for this position is October 2026; however, this is an estimate and may be revised if needed. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Offers are determined based on a review of the candidate's qualifications, including education, training, experience, and internal pay equity considerations. Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors: Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position. Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role. Upper Range: Candidates with seven or more years of directly related experience, advanced knowledge, specialized skills, certifications, or expertise that provide significant value to the position. Placement above the minimum rate will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources. Position Type: Staff Required Education: Bachelor’s degree in a related discipline. Required Work Experience: At least 3 years of related work experience in an educational institution, workshop, or model-making facility. Required Licenses and Certifications: Physical Demands: Bending Carrying Electrical Hazards Moving Reaching Sitting Twisting Climbing Lifting Pulling/Pushing Repetitive movement Standing Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered: Master’s degree preferred in fine arts, sculpture, furniture design, or industrial design. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Prepare and administer the Woodshop budget. Participate in relevant ad hoc committees or committees relevant to the wood shop area. Develop and implement a wood shop training program for faculty, staff, and students. Train and manage student work-study. Develop and implement a centralized tool storage and security check-out system. Maintain a safe and clean shop environment. Monitor the maintenance and adjustments of power and hand tools. Ensure adherence to all shop equipment safety regulations. Maintain woodshop hours and days to fulfill the instructional and student course needs of each semester. Advise shop users on the safe use of tools and machines. Consult and advise shop users on best practices based on project needs and materials. Maintain and revise shop policies. Compile and maintain shop tool and equipment inventory. Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Supports, promotes, and develops university student enrollment and retention initiatives. Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. Marginal Duties/Responsibilities: Produce light project construction throughout the building. Produce light classroom furniture construction. Skills and Abilities: Ability to maintain all stationary power tools associated with a woodshop, including changing planar/jointer knives, setting up vacuum bags/tables, CNC machine, etc. Ability to operate across both analog and digital methods of making. Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript 1 Optional Documents: Special Instructions to Applicants: Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of their degree. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript. Unofficial Transcript 2 (OPTIONAL): Applicants who have completed college coursework or attained a degree must attach a copy of their unofficial transcript. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript. Initial Application Review Date: September 28, 2026 Open Until Position is Filled?: Yes Posting Close Date: EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Click here to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498229/ace-training-lab-assistant-student-position": {
      "title": "ACE Training Lab Assistant (Student Position)",
      "description": "ACE Training Lab Assistant (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498229 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: ACE Training Lab Assistant (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: College of Engineering Technology Advertised Salary: $20 Summary of Position: Check in and out tools, maintain inventory, for Manufacturing Engineering Machining Laboratory Tool Crib. Assist faculty in various duties related to Machining Laboratory, assist students in machining process, practice safe working habits. Position Requirements: Student must have previously taken manufacturing courses within the Manufacturing Engineering program Essential Duties/Responsibilities: knowledge of feed and speed calculations, safe working habits, measuring instruments, and CNC programing Number of Positions Available: 2 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: October 30, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
