    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498190/stageauditorium-assistant-level-i-student-position": {
      "title": "Stage/Auditorium Assistant Level I (Student Position)",
      "description": "Stage/Auditorium Assistant Level I (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498190 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Stage/Auditorium Assistant Level I (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Department: College of Arts and Sciences Advertised Salary: $13.73 Summary of Position: Williams Auditorium is seeking a dependable, motivated student worker to join our event operations team. This position provides hands-on experience in live events, concerts, theater, lectures, conferences, performances, and other programs held at Williams Auditorium. This is a great opportunity for students interested in theater, music, event planning, production, communications, hospitality, entertainment, or live events, but no previous technical experience is required. Position Requirements: Required: • Dependable and able to arrive on time for scheduled shifts • Willingness to learn and work as part of a team • Ability to follow directions and safety procedures • Positive and professional attitude • Ability to perform physical tasks associated with event setup and teardown Preferred, but not required: • Interest or experience in theater, music, events, production, or entertainment • Previous experience with stage equipment, lighting, audio, or video • Customer service or hospitality experience • Ability to work independently once trained Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Student workers may assist with a wide variety of tasks, including: • Setting up and tearing down events • Moving and arranging tables, chairs, staging, and other equipment • Assisting with stage and backstage preparations • Helping with basic lighting, audio, and video equipment • Assisting with microphones and presentation equipment • Supporting concerts, theater productions, lectures, conferences, ceremonies, and special events • Assisting performers, speakers, presenters, and event clients • Helping with audience seating and event logistics • Preparing dressing rooms, backstage areas, and event spaces • Operating or assisting with basic venue equipment after appropriate training • Loading and unloading event equipment and materials • Maintaining clean, organized, and safe event spaces • Assisting with event transitions and room changes • Providing general event support before, during, and after events • Following venue safety procedures and event-specific instructions • Performing other duties related to auditorium and event operations as assigned • Scenic Construction and/ or painting assistance for university productions Number of Positions Available: 3 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Cover Letter Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 28 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498165/violence-prevent-peer-educator-student-position": {
      "title": "Violence Prevent Peer Educator (Student Position)",
      "description": "Violence Prevent Peer Educator (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498165 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503, Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Violence Prevention Peer Educator (Student Position) Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49307 Department: 60- VP Student Affairs Advertised Salary: $13.73- $14.00 Summary of Position: The Anti-Violence Alliance office is seeking a student to assist them with creating new prevention initiatives and to amplify existing efforts on campus. This position is relevant for students pursuing degrees in communications, criminal justice, graphic design, social sciences, or women's studies. Position Requirements: *Must display a commitment to sexual and relationship violence issues *A passion and desire to make a difference *Have a desire to learn about university prevention organizations and practices *Must be organized, have strong attention to detail, and be able to complete projects independently *Be enrolled at Ferris State University, taking at least 6 credits *Maintain at least a 2.0 GPA *Have approval from the Office of Student Community Standards to join the program Essential Duties/Responsibilities: *Generate a curriculum of events that would occur throughout the academic year *Provide year-round awareness to ensure that changes in thoughts and actions are sustained long-term *Attend all monthly Anti-Violence Alliance meetings *Attend all mandatory training sessions (Including but not limited to dating/domestic violence, sexual assault, stalking, public speaking, prevention best practices, how to facilitate the Bringing in the Bystander curriculum, and annual refresher training ) * Co-facilitate prevention/awareness programs or events each semester *We are looking mainly for peer educators who are willing to present, but we can accept a few applicants who only want to create social media content. Number of Positions Available: 3 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: 09/16/2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 27 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
