    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498097/it-application-programmer-asst-student-position": {
      "title": "IT Application Programmer Asst (Student Position)",
      "description": "IT Application Programmer Asst (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498097 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: IT Applications Programmer (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: IT Services Advertised Salary: $13.73- $13.99 Summary of Position: Learning the different SQL and Oracle databases, web design and programming. Position Requirements: - Need to be a team player - Preferred experience in HTML or programming language or database query and/or design - Must be able to multitask - Preferred student in their 2nd or 3rd year at Ferris Essential Duties/Responsibilities: - Wil be a continued position with added responsibilities given they advance through their studies. - Assist with creating reports or data feeds from Oracle or SQL table, Assist on webpage upgrades, Assist in testing of upgrades, Assist with creating reports using WebFocus reporting tool, Assist with documentation on tasks or projects. - This is Monday – Friday position with the office open 8:00am to 5:00pm. Number of Positions Available: 1 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: November 1, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 12 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 01 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498093/student-printmaking-studio-monitor-student-position": {
      "title": "Student Printmaking Studio Monitor (Student Position)",
      "description": "Student Printmaking Studio Monitor (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498093 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Student Printmaking Studio Monitor (Student Position) Location: Grand Rapids, MI Department: Kendall College of Art and Design Advertised Salary: $14 Summary of Position: Supervise use of manual presses and work areas during open studio hours. Supervise use of manual presses and work areas during open studio hours. Position Type: Student Position Position Requirements: One year of experience working the KCAD’s Printmaking Studio. Must be familiar with intaglio, relief, screen printing, and monotype processes. Good communication skills: must be able to answer student questions and explain printmaking methods clearly. The ability to work with a diverse group of printmaking students and faculty in a courteous and professional manner. Must be reliable, punctual, and able to work with minimal supervision. Must be currently enrolled full or part-time student at Ferris State University's Kendall College of Art and Design. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: One year of experience working the KCAD’s Printmaking Studio. Must be familiar with intaglio, relief, screen printing, and monotype processes. Good communication skills: must be able to answer student questions and explain printmaking methods clearly. The ability to work with a diverse group of printmaking students and faculty in a courteous and professional manner. Must be reliable, punctual, and able to work with minimal supervision. Must be currently enrolled full or part-time student at Ferris State University's Kendall College of Art and Design. Number of Positions Available: 2 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that