    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/497909/workshop-tutor-1-student-position": {
      "title": "Workshop Tutor 1 (Student Position)",
      "description": "Workshop Tutor 1 (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 497909 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Workshop Tutor 1 (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Department: University College Advertised Salary: $13.73 Summary of Position: A workshop tutor provides academic support through workshop sessions focused on specific courses or topics. This role involves leading or assisting workshops that review key concepts, reinforce course material, and help students prepare for assignments and exams. Workshop tutors help students learn by providing focused, interactive learning activities in a group setting. Workshops take place in a classroom provided by the department or professor for up to two hours per day. The Workshop Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content. This position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty. This position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location. Student employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support. Position Type: Student Position Requirements: *Must have a GPA of 2.75 or higher *Must have completed the course they will be assisting with and earned a grade of B or higher *For math tutoring, must have completed Math 130 *Must demonstrate excellent communication and organizational skills *Must be hired through HR prior to beginning tutoring duties Essential Duties/Responsibilities: *Will assist students with coursework in various subject areas in a workshop setting *For questions or concerns outside of the position summary requested by faculty, please direct your questions to the Director *Workshop tutors are required to take attendance in Navigate for every workshop tutoring session Number of Positions Available: 10 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Class Schedule, Cover Letter (optional) Job Close Date: December 18, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 03 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 18 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/497990/pharmacology-research-assistant-student-position": {
      "title": "Pharmacology Research Assistant (Student Position)",
      "description": "Pharmacology Research Assistant (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 497990 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Pharmacology Research Assistant (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Department: College of Pharmacy Advertised Salary: $13.73 Summary of Position: This position will be supported by Md Afjalus Siraj, PhD Ferris Research Grant, 2026. The student Research Assistant will work on how combination therapy, like SMNDC1 inhibitor along with KRAS inhibitor, overcome targeted therapy resistance in pancreatic cancer. Position Requirements: Current student of Ferris State University with a major in Forensic Biology, Biotechnology, Biochemistry Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Design and revise laboratory protocols In hand cell based assay development Lab note maintenance and regular discussion with PI Attend weekly lab meeting Discuss with PI about other weekly responsibilities Literature review and data extraction Data analysis Number of Positions Available: 1 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Cover Letter Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 03 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
