    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/497991/kcad-flex-lab-asst-student-position": {
      "title": "KCAD Flex Lab Asst (Student Position)",
      "description": "KCAD Flex Lab Asst (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 497991 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Grand Rapids, MI 49503 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: KCAD FlexLab Assistant (Student Position) Location: Grand Rapids, MI Department: Kendall College of Art and Design Advertised Salary: $13.73- $13.99 Summary of Position: FlexLab student employees work directly with the Dow Center FlexLab Coordinator. Students will learn new skills and technologies on the job to facilitate the successful output of digital fabrication/design projects with the KCAD/FSU community. Weekly schedule will be decided based on the student's availability, the FlexLab's staffing needs, and open lab hours. Hours are somewhat flexible and work around the student's course schedule as it changes from semester to semester. Position Requirements: *Must have retail or service industry experience *Experience and working knowledge of Adobe Creative Cloud *A willingness to learn on the job *Experience with or interest to learn the use of 2D and 3D input and output devices Essential Duties/Responsibilities: *Communicate effectively with the Coordinator and the KCAD/FSU Campus at large *Track material and technology usage and supply prompt reporting *Cash handling via cash, check, credit card *Learn and teach FlexLab processes to FlexLab users *Operate equipment including wide format inkjet printers, 3D scanners, 3D printers, vinyl cutters, and LASER cutters/engravers *Learn and understand the pros and cons of each process *Accurately record and calculate billing and usage data *Projects as assigned by coordinator Number of Positions Available: 1 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Cover Letter/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to cultivating an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences within its community, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 01 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/497992/golf-shop-assistant-student-position": {
      "title": "Golf Shop Assistant (Student Position)",
      "description": "Golf Shop Assistant (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 497992 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Golf Shop Assistant (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: Katke Golf Course Advertised Salary: $13.73 Summary of Position: Golf shop assistant will be helping in the shop and checking in guess with tee times. Working in the Pro Shop and Janke Learning center Position Requirements: - Prefer background and knowledge of retail operations and golf knowledge is beneficial. - As an individual who is responsible for driving on behalf of the university, a driving record check will be run pursuant to university policies. The individual will be required to sign an authorization to run a criminal history background and driving record check. - Safe driving is mandatory at all times while operating a golf cart on the course. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: - Assisting with tournament operations - Answering phone calls - Assisting members and guests with tee times and check in upon arrival - Receiving, restocking and displaying of merchandise, - Cash handling and operating a point of sale system - Setting up customers with Trackman bays - Indoor and outdoor range ball coverage - Maintaining organization and light cleaning of all areas. - Operates university motor vehicles, including golf carts, safely while carrying out job responsibilities. - Staging carts in the morning and throughout the day. Taking carts from the barn to the staging area. - Using carts to manage the course- Ranger duties, assist customers when needed - Returning carts to the wash area and parking in the barn to recharge. - Pick Balls from the range- Return balls to wash and fill the ball dispenser - Set up course for events - Driving golf carts on public roads is strictly prohibited. Number of Positions Available: 8 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: October 31, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 01 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
