    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498320/asc-office-assistant-student-position": {
      "title": "ASC Office Assistant (Student Position)",
      "description": "ASC Office Assistant (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498320 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: ASC Office Assistant Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: ASC Office Assistant Advertised Salary: $13.73-$13.99 Summary of Position: The Office Assistant position exists to support students as they enter the Tutoring Center and help create a welcoming, organized, and efficient environment. This role is located at the front desk of the Tutoring Center within the Academic Literacies Center. Position Requirements: Experience using Microsoft Office applications such as Word or Excel Experience with Navigate is preferred but not required Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Position duties include • Answering phones and updating voicemail as needed • Responding to emails • Scheduling appointments in Navigate • Filing and organizing • Updating webpages • Preparing for events • Maintaining supply inventory • Assisting students who enter the ALC • Photocopying, checking the copy machine for paper and troubleshooting other issues that may occur • Provide support to tutors and faculty by answering questions as needed • Assisting the secretary and direct with various duties • Other duties, as assigned Number of Positions Available: 1 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Class Schedule, Cover Letter (optional) Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498346/admissions-clerical-i-student-position": {
      "title": "Admissions Clerical I (Student Position)",
      "description": "Admissions Clerical I (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498346 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Admissions Clerical I (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: Admissions Advertised Salary: $13.73-$13.99 Summary of Position: Join the Office in Admissions in moving prospective students Ferris Forward by providing exceptional customer service, assisting the processing team with incoming transcripts and providing office support. Position Requirements: Minimal experience in Microsoft Teams, customer service, and a positive attitude. Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Processing transcripts, processing projects, customer service, office support, and visit assistance. Number of Positions Available: 6 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume/ Class Schedule Job Close Date: January 15, 2027 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence. Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 15 Jan 2027 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
